<title>UK: Austria adds 25 million marks to 10-year bond.</title>
<headline>Austria adds 25 million marks to 10-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following fixed/reverse FRN bond has been increased to 125 million marks from 100 million marks lead manager Morgan Stanley Frankfurt said on Tuesday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   AUSTRIA</p>
<p> AMT    125 MLN DEM   COUPON   * 8.00	MATURITY    21.MAR.07</p>
<p> TYPE   FIXED/FRN     ISS PRICE  100.0     PAY DATE  **29.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REC REOFF  98.38     SPREAD	=</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    FFT	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) ONE	 SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   NO</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  AUSTRIA   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.375     SELL CONC  1.625     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES   * YEARS 1-3, 16.25 PCT MINUS 2 TIMES 6MLIBOR THEREAFTER</p>
<p>	  ** PLUS 38 DAYS ACCRUED INTEREST</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
